# .gitignore -- cm-outbound-bench
#
# Two data classes live in this repository and they are treated differently:
#
#   * APPROVED PROCESSED RESEARCH DATA is tracked. The private research
#     repository for supervisor review contains the processed decision-point
#     Task datasets, the split artifacts, the frozen LLM-Gold references and the
#     Group A evaluation records. Those paths are therefore NOT ignored -- see
#     "Tracked by design" below, which spells out the boundary so that no broad
#     pattern silently swallows them again.
#
#   * RAW AND UNPUBLISHABLE DATA is never tracked: the original TXT transcript
#     export, the de-identified corpus that is stored outside this repository,
#     raw audio, confidential databases, credentials and local tool caches.
#
# Rule of thumb for editors: add narrow, path-specific ignores. Never add
# `data/`, `outputs/`, `*.jsonl`, `*.json` or `*.sqlite` style blanket rules.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python environments
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
.venv*/
venv/
env/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python build, cache and coverage artifacts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
# pytest creates its tmp_path base in the working directory on some Windows
# setups; those directories contain generated scratch data only.
pytest-of-*/
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local secrets -- never commit
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
providers.toml
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.enc

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Raw and unapproved corpus data -- never commit
#
# The raw TXT export and the `cm_outbound_v2` de-identified corpus are stored
# OUTSIDE this repository under <project-parent>/data/. These rules are the
# in-repository belt-and-braces guard: if such a directory is ever copied into
# the working tree it must not be committed by accident. Benchmark code must
# never open the raw export (docs/data_privacy.md section 2).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/TXT/
data/raw/
data/raw_txt/
data/interim/
data/private/
data/secure/
data/entity_maps/
data/deidentified/
data/rejected/
data/corpus_db/
data/audio/

# Raw audio recordings.
*.wav
*.mp3
*.m4a
*.amr
*.silk

# Confidential corpus databases. `data/decision/` ships only JSON/JSONL, so no
# legitimate publication artifact is a SQLite file; the corpus database and any
# journal/write-ahead file stay local.
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite-journal
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm
cm_outbound_corpus.sqlite

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local runtime scratch (not research evidence)
#
# The release evidence under outputs/ IS tracked, including the Milestone 1.2
# Group A artifacts under outputs/decision/. Only per-machine working
# directories and local debugging output are ignored here.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
logs/
/*.log
outputs/tmp/
outputs/local/
outputs/review/
outputs/corpus/
outputs/debug/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OS and editor metadata
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*.tmp

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tracked by design -- do not add ignore rules for these paths
#
#   src/                      benchmark, corpus, transcripts, decisions, gold
#   tests/                    unit, integration and isolation tests
#   configs/                  dataset, split, baseline agent, judge config
#   prompts/                  frozen annotation and scoring prompts
#   data/tasks/               legacy synthetic Tasks  (Agent-visible, synthetic)
#   data/policy/              legacy synthetic policy documents
#   data/synthetic/           legacy synthetic runtime database and states
#   data/decision/tasks/      Agent-visible decision-point Tasks + private refs
#   data/decision/calls/      reconstructed de-identified conversations
#   data/decision/splits/     call-level split manifest (seed, duplicate groups)
#   data/decision/samples/    fixed annotation/evaluation sample plans
#   data/decision/annotations/annotation packets + manifests
#   data/decision/business_sources/  business reference inventory
#   outputs/decision/annotations/    frozen Gold Labels, passes, adjudications
#   outputs/decision/evaluation/     blind Group A scoring records
#   outputs/decision/traces/         Group A execution traces
#   outputs/decision/reports/        aggregate Group A reports
#   outputs/live_llm_*/, outputs/runs/  legacy synthetic validation evidence
#
# Every one of those paths is an approved Class 1 / Class 2 research artifact;
# see docs/reports/github_dataset_upload_manifest.md for the per-file decision.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
